FILE: assets/css/timeLineList.css
FEATURE: timeline-list-verification
DATE: 2026-10-05
PRIOR STATE: commit 3f1472a (unchanged since it was added; never linked by any code until this change)

================================================================================
CHANGE 1 — room for the label column
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
.vtimeLine {
    border-left: solid 1px #710943;
    padding-left: 23px;
    list-style-type: none !important;
}

NEW_SECTION
.vtimeLine {
    border-left: solid 1px #710943;
    padding-left: 23px;
    margin-left: 110px; /* room for the label column drawn to the left of the line */
    list-style-type: none !important;
}

REASON
Labels are drawn at left:-133px from each <li>, about 109px left of the rail. With no margin, a
list at the page edge put its labels off-screen (verified: 0px of room). This never showed because
the file was never loaded. Now that the module links it, the default has to render. No consumer
can depend on the old value, since the file was never applied.

================================================================================
CHANGE 2 — wrap rules: three classes, and the margin dropped when stacked
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
/* Wrap styles */
.vtimeLine.wrap li{
    padding-top: 23px;
    
}

.vtimeLine.wrap li::after{
    left: -14px;
    text-align: left;
}

NEW_SECTION
/* Wrap styles: three classes, so they outrank a list's own generated styles (two classes) */
.vtimeLine.activated.wrap{
    margin-left: 0;
}
.vtimeLine.activated.wrap li{
    padding-top: 23px;
    
}

.vtimeLine.activated.wrap li::after{
    left: -14px;
    text-align: left;
}

REASON
In stacked mode the labels sit above the entries, so the 110px label margin must go. Generated
per-list rules now use two classes so they beat the one-class defaults (see the module log, change
6). The wrap rules move to three classes so the stacked layout still repositions a list whose own
label style sets `left`. Verified: the label at -14px with a list style of left:-200px, and the
list's label colour still applied.
